<Document title="Set up ZEC Buying Price on your Mac" description="Install the Apple Silicon development DMG, import a mainnet Unified Full Viewing Key, choose a birthday, and review acquisition prices."><h2>Install the development build</h2><p><a href="/download/">Download .dmg</a>, open the disk image, and drag ZECBuyingPrice into Applications. Version {site.version} requires an Apple Silicon Mac with Secure Enclave support and macOS 14 or later. {release.notarized ? 'It is Developer ID signed and notarized by Apple, with a stapled notarization ticket.' : release.signed ? 'It is Developer ID signed and is not notarized by Apple; Gatekeeper acceptance has not been verified. Check release details before opening it.' : 'Packaging and signing checks are pending; check release details before downloading.'}</p><p>Open the app from Applications after reviewing its signing status on the release page. {release.notarized ? 'Confirm the standard macOS prompt for an app downloaded from the internet.' : 'macOS may require additional approval for a build that is signed but not notarized.'} You can verify the download against the <a href="/releases/">published checksum</a>. For installation questions, follow <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">Apple’s guidance for opening apps from outside the App Store</a>. Managed Macs may apply additional installation policies.</p><h2>Import a viewing key</h2><p>Obtain a mainnet Unified Full Viewing Key using your wallet’s supported export method. Paste it into the app’s setup screen. A public receiving address is not a UFVK. The app does not request a seed phrase or spending key.</p><img src="/images/setup.webp" width="1100" height="803" alt="ZEC Buying Price wallet setup with a viewing-key field and wallet birthday controls" loading="lazy" /><h2>Choose the wallet birthday</h2><p>Set a date before the wallet’s first activity. If you know a suitable birthday block height, the optional height takes precedence. The SDK uses available checkpoints, so scanning may begin earlier than the date or height you enter.</p><h2>Check network and price settings</h2><p>In Settings, review the TLS lightwalletd endpoint. The default is <code>zec.rocks:443</code>. You can also configure optional CoinGecko Demo or Pro API access. Older history may require paid access or manual prices.</p><h2>Authenticate and start scanning</h2><p>Authenticate with Touch ID or your Mac login password, then start the scan. Transactions appear as the SDK discovers and enhances them. The provisional acquisition value and average use discovered movements with available receipt prices and update as syncing and pricing continue. The full average still requires completed scanning and every selected receipt price. Check each movement’s inclusion checkbox, then click its USD-per-ZEC price to enter an actual acquisition price where you have a record.</p><p>The scan bar follows the SDK’s work percentage. Block details show completed blocks scanned, the chain tip, and the height through which history is fully verified. The SDK can scan newer ranges first, so the verified height can pause while the scan count and percentage advance.</p><p>Syncing continues when you switch apps, hide the app, or minimize the window; the wallet interface locks until you authenticate again. Closing the last wallet window, quitting, sleeping, or locking the Mac stops the worker and closes protected storage.</p><p>Do not interpret the screenshot’s synthetic data as a completed scan for your wallet. Read <a href="/blog/incomplete-zcash-average/">incomplete-result troubleshooting</a> if inputs remain unresolved.</p><h2>Keep your research private</h2><p>The viewing key is encrypted using Secure Enclave protection. Wallet history and choices stay in an encrypted disk image under <code>~/Library/Application Support/ZECBuyingPrice/protected-vault/</code>. The optional price API key remains in Keychain. A viewing key reveals financial history, even without spending authority. Read <a href="/privacy/">privacy and network behavior</a> before sharing logs or screenshots.</p></Document>
